Thumbnails of unmarked pictures in the shape of a pair are made again: stereo-layer takes an unmarked picture within
2:1 to 3.6:1 for a side by side pair by its shape (ORDER 504), so the image and JPEG thumbnailers' versions go up
(3 to 4 and 5 to 6) and flat thumbnails cached before are remade.

Built against, and depending on, the stereo layer that holds the person's per-file 3D choice (stereo-layer 1.18.0,
ORDER 512 and 551): the thumbnail worker shows a file as its entry in $XDG_STATE_HOME/stereo-policy/files says, the
same as Dolphin and Gwenview. The build stops with CMake's message when the layer is older
(CMAKE_REQUIRE_FIND_PACKAGE_StereoLayer).
